{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:22-3","provision":"BCO 22-3","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"22-3","title":"Section 22-3","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/22-3/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/22-3","current_text":{"html":"<p>An assistant pastor is called by the Session, by the permission and approval of Presbytery, under the provisions of <i>BCO</i> 20-1 and 13-2, with Presbytery membership being governed by the same provisions that apply to pastors. He is not a member of the Session, but may be appointed on special occasions to moderate the Session under the provisions of <i>BCO</i> 12-4.</p>","text":"An assistant pastor is called by the Session, by the permission and approval of Presbytery, under the provisions of BCO 20-1 and 13-2, with Presbytery membership being governed by the same provisions that apply to pastors. He is not a member of the Session, but may be appointed on special occasions to moderate the Session under the provisions of BCO 12-4."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"94a0b54eec213ad53deb08f9fe4e387f46d90e3373f4cd38647b018d7b192c88","parent_id":"bco:22","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":14,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:22-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga49_2022__ci01.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga49_2022__ci01.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Assistant Pastor standing to file complaints against Sessions","year":2022,"disposition":"in conflict; Adopted by the CCB","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga49_2022__ci01.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga49_2022__ci01.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga49_2022__ci01.md:occ-51ae012c61b8","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga49_2022__ci01.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga49_2022__ci01.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"CCB found an overture allowing assistant pastors to file complaints against Sessions under BCO 22-3 to be in conflict with the BCO.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga49_2022__ci01.md"}]},{"id":"bco:22-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Relationship of Assistant Pastor to the Church","year":2005,"disposition":"in conflict","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md:occ-c296624e5f24","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"An overture detailing how assistant pastors are called was found in conflict with BCO 3-2 and 12-2 through 12-4, as the relationship of an assistant pastor to a congregation is best left to the session.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md"}]},{"id":"bco:22-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Implementation of 1988 BCO amendments on Assistant Pastors","year":1989,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md:occ-65748ff5403e","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"Tennessee Valley Presbytery asked whether the new BCO 22-3/22-4 Assistant Pastor provisions applied retroactively, to all full-time ministers, and whether a lesser examination was appropriate.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci03.md"}]},{"id":"bco:22-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Call of assistant pastor from another denomination without presbyterial examination","year":1986,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md:occ-4c3ab877ab72","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"A session may not call an ordained assistant pastor from another denomination without presbytery approval and examination, as all teaching elders must be members of the serving presbytery.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md"}]},{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Bigelow v. North Florida Presbytery","year":2025,"disposition":"granted","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md:occ-ad367197d2af","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":269},"excerpt":"…their Assistant Pastor. In that case the Session of CCE is the calling body (BCO 22-3) and thus the Session of CCE is the body that had the right to petition Presbytery to dissolve the relationship (BCO 22-4).","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["call dissolution","assistant pastor","church planting","mission church","pastoral relationship","discipline without process","mediation commission","BCO 43 complaint","BCO 23-1","congregational vote","provisional session","BCO 5 mission church","dissolution of pastoral call","congregational rights","mediation","nondisclosure agreement","contumacy","BCO 12-5-e session pulpit authority","women preaching","call dissolution procedure","mission church governance"],"case_numbers":["2024-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"TE Kevin Bigelow complained against multiple actions of North Florida Presbytery related to the dissolution of his call as Assistant Pastor of Christ Church East (where he was also serving as planting pastor at Christ Church Beaches). The SJC sustained the complaint in part (22-0-0), finding that Presbytery erred in…"}},{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"David Kniseley et al. v. Rocky Mountain Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-3540d9c8ce30","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":80},"excerpt":"\"In light of the ratification of item #18 (amendments to BCO 22-3 and 22-4)..","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"},{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-20020625dfb0","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":90},"excerpt":"2. No. Only those assistant pastors as defined above need to comply with the provisions of BCO 22-3 and 4... Adopted","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"},{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-732447e8486b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":246},"excerpt":"We recommend that the GA clarify the BCO regarding this subject (e.g. BCO 22-3 says an assistant pastor is not a member of the session, yet 12-4 says he may moderate the session; 22-3 indicates the call is by the session, yet 22-4 and 23-1 indicate that the…","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"},{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-bab86d5f9b9e","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":258},"excerpt":"1. BCO 22-3 shall read: An Assistant Pastor is called by the Session, by the permission and approval of Presbytery, under the provisions of chapter 20, 21 and 13-2, with presbytery membership being governed by the same provisions that apply to Pastors. He is…","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"},{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-e134c59330c9","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":264},"excerpt":"…BCO (M16GA, Knoxville, 1988, p. 109). This has continued to be the language of BCO 22-3 and 22-4 since 1988. After the 16th GA, Tennessee Valley filed their inquiry (which the SJC now references in their Reasoning). However, the full text of the TVP inquiry…","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"},{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-9af5a2550832","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":266},"excerpt":"Q: In light of the [change to BCO 22-3 and 22-4]... our questions are:","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"},{"id":"bco:22-3--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-aeba85c10fd5","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":282},"excerpt":"2. No. Only those assistant pastors as defined above need to comply with the provisions of BCO 22-3 and 4.","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["minister title","non-ordained staff","women","constitutional interpretation","presbytery judgment"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-13"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"On complaint from TE David Kniseley and others, the SJC reviewed Rocky Mountain Presbytery's refusal to forbid a mission church from giving an unordained female staff member the title 'Minister of Church Life.' The SJC denied the complaint. It held the BCO uses 'minister' synonymously with pastor and teaching elder, but is silent on general use for non-ordained staff; a lower court may exercise discretion subject to BCO 40-2(3)'s WESP review. The decision addressed only the constitutional issue, not the title's wisdom or propriety; four commissioners dissented."}},{"id":"bco:22-3--overture:ga49_2022:2","record_id":"overture:ga49_2022:2","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 22-3 to Allow Assistant Pastors to File Complaints Against Sessions","year":2022,"disposition":"","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga49_2022.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga49_2022.md","evidence_basis":"title_subject_reference","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-3--overture:ga49_2022:2:occ-0a223cca1995","url":"https://